the minutes after a gunman opened fire  in a Frankfort suburb he targeted a  shisha bar popular with immigrants and  police are now looking into what appears  to be a racist killing spree in the  heart of Germany today the midnight bar  in hano remained sealed off for scenes  of crimes officers scoured the premises  where the first of what would become  nine people died those inside had no  defense against an armed man intent on  killing and maiming interior minister  horsey hopper visited the scene of what  would be just the first horrific attack  in Hanna as the public prosecutor  identified the gunman as Thomas R a 43  year old German who was tracked to this  apartment where he was found dead along  with his 72 year old mother a video  online postings and documents found at  the flat point to what the federal  prosecutor called a deeply racist  mindset he had gone on to target another  location killing four inside this cafe  and shooting another person in a car  saad jan heard the gunfire and rushed  outside he was horrified by what he saw  people he knew lying dead I was in the  house and I heard three shots and I  heard more shots and I ran to the kiosk  and then I saw the injured people locals  came to lay flowers close to the cafe  barely able to believe what had happened  just yards away the body of one of the  victims was being removed as discreetly  as possible the attacks are being  treated as an act of domestic terrorism  German Chancellor Angela Merkel reacting  to the evidence of racist killings much  currently indicates that the perpetrator  acted out far-right racist motives  fueled by hate against  with different backgrounds a different  religion or different appearance racism  is a poison the investigation is now  focusing on whether the gunman acted  alone or whether he had co-conspirators  and supporters the federal police are  examining the video and notes found at  his apartment because Germans  contemplate what looks like homegrown  terrorism the country's president led  the morning at the two sites where  people were killed and injured attacks  which left many immigrants wondering if  they're safe here  Michelle Clifford Sky News Hannah  Germany
 

